=task S36CR-006
status: done

I notice this in the output:

togetl:document:53132fa64afac23f L36C1...L36C111 3dparts:part:p1060 3dparts:stlFile urn:bitprint:R7AGQHKFTNMWJQ352KZS4W4FSYH3KJFO.BGAOZL4H7UPECXJTRCLJXSYJDBY6LHLQY33NPTI
togetl:document:53132fa64afac23f L36C1...L36C111 urn:bitprint:R7AGQHKFTNMWJQ352KZS4W4FSYH3KJFO.BGAOZL4H7UPECXJTRCLJXSYJDBY6LHLQY33NPTI general:filename data:,p1060-TGx7.stl
togetl:document:53132fa64afac23f L36C1...L36C111 urn:bitprint:R7AGQHKFTNMWJQ352KZS4W4FSYH3KJFO.BGAOZL4H7UPECXJTRCLJXSYJDBY6LHLQY33NPTI rdf:type togetl:File

urn:bitprint:R7AGQHKFTNMWJQ352KZS4W4FSYH3KJFO.BGAOZL4H7UPECXJTRCLJXSYJDBY6LHLQY33NPTI refers to a specific byte sequence ('blob').
The byte sequence doesn't inherently have a name.
Furthermore, multiple 'parts' could refer to the same blob by different names!

So we need to separate the concept of the 'file' (which has a name)
from the blob identified by the bitprint hash.

